{title: 533 - O for a Faith}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[G]O, for [D7]a[G]faith that will not [D]shrink,
Though [G]pressed by [D]man[A7]y a [D]foe,
[D]That [G]will not [Em]tremble [C]on the [D7]brink of [G]poverty,
Of [D7]poverty or [G]woe; Of po[C]ver[G]ty [D7]or [G]woe;

Verse 2:
[G]That [D7]will not [G]murmur [D]or complain
[G]Beneath [D]the [A7]chastening [D]rod,
[D]But in [G]the hour [Em]of grief [C]or pain, [D7]of grief [G]or pain
[D7]Can [G]lean upon [C]its God; [G]Can [D7]lean upon [G]its God.

Verse 3:
[G]A faith [D7]that shines [G]more bright [D]and clear
[G]When [D]tempests [A7]rage [D]without;
[D]That [G]when in [Em]danger knows [C]no fear, [D7]knows of [G]no fear,
[D7]In [G]darkness feels [C]no doubt; [G]In [D7]darkness feels [G]no doubt.

Verse 4:
[G]That [D7]bears unmoved [G]the world's [D]dread frown,
[G]Nor [D]heeds [A7]its [D]scornful smile;
[D]That [G]sin's wild [Em]ocean [C]cannot drown, [D7]no, [G]cannot drown,
[D7]Nor [G]its soft [C]arts beguile; [G]Nor [D7]its soft [G]arts beguile.

Verse 5:
[G]Lord, give [D7]me such [G]a faith [D]as this,
[G]And [D]then, [A7]whate'er [D]may come
[D]I'll [G]taste, e'en [Em]here the [C]hallowed [D7]bliss, the [G]hallowed bliss
[D7]Of [G]an [C]eternal home; [G]Of [D7]an [G]eternal home.
